For a four-dimensional Schwarzschild black hole, $R_s=2G_NM,
\qquad
A=4\pi R_s^2.$ Dropping $2$ and $4\pi$ as the lecture does, $\begin{aligned}
S_{\mathrm{BH}}
&\sim \frac{R_s^2}{G_N}
\sim \frac{(G_NM)^2}{G_N} \\
&\sim M^2G_N
\sim M^2\ell_p^2.
\end{aligned}$ This is the form we shall compare with a string count.

